# Watch boundary

This repo is two-mobile: the watch and its companion iPhone. It is not the development-loop GUI.

- Talk only to `https://<enrolled-host>:8443`. Refuse loopback and port `8741`.
- Principal is `client:watch`. Profiles are `chat`, `home-action`, or omitted. Never `self-build` or `operator`.
- Never `POST /v1/tasks`. Never pause, resume, cancel, config, artifact content, or `tasks:message`.
- Never set `X-Two-Edge-Token`, `X-Two-Client-Id`, or `Authorization`. The bearer slot stays empty.
- Do not put `TWO_API_TOKEN`, `TWO_EDGE_TOKEN`, a PKCS#12, `ca.crt`, or a LAN address in source or git.
- Pin the enrolled CA. Unknown trust challenges are cancelled. Client-certificate challenges use only the enrolled identity.

```swift
// ❌ BAD
request.setValue(token, forHTTPHeaderField: "Authorization")
url = URL(string: "https://127.0.0.1:8741")!

// ✅ GOOD
if let bearer = DeferredBearer.headerValue(), !bearer.isEmpty {
    request.setValue("Bearer \(bearer)", forHTTPHeaderField: "Authorization")
}
```
